Consider an axisymmetric, vertically-integrated protoplanetary disc model in which a planet of mass M_p orbits at radius r_p in a gas disc of surface density Σ_g(r,t), temperature T(r), and turbulent viscosity parameter α. The planet opens a gap whose depth and width are determined by M_p, α, and the local disc aspect ratio h/r. Embedded in the gas is a population of dust grains described by a size distribution n(a, r, t) (with a the grain radius), evolving under the coupled processes of:

(i) radial drift driven by gas pressure gradients, with drift velocity v_drift(a, r) depending on the Stokes number St(a, r) and ∂P/∂r;
(ii) turbulent and differential-drift induced collisions producing coagulation up to a fragmentation barrier a_frag(r) set by a fragmentation velocity v_frag and α;
(iii) fragmentation cascades that replenish small grains;
(iv) opacity κ_ν(a) that, combined with the dust column, determines the emergent spectral energy distribution (SED) and millimetre-wavelength flux F_mm.

The transition-disc SED constraint requires that the small-grain (a ≲ a few μm) population in an inner region r < r_cav be reduced sufficiently to suppress near-infrared excess, while the millimetre flux F_mm and resolved mm emission morphology agree with observations of transition discs and the configuration persists on a timescale comparable to the disc lifetime τ_disc ∼ 10^6–10^7 yr.

Question. Determine whether there exists a non-empty region of the parameter space (M_p, r_p, α, Σ_g, h/r, v_frag, dust-to-gas ratio, κ_ν) consistent with realistic protoplanetary disc conditions for which the coupled drift–coagulation–fragmentation evolution of n(a, r, t), with self-consistent opacities, simultaneously:

(a) converts enough small dust into larger particles inside or near the planet-induced gap to reproduce the observed near-infrared deficit of transition-disc SEDs;
(b) does not over- or under-produce the observed millimetre continuum flux and spatial distribution; and
(c) maintains conditions (a) and (b) over a duration comparable to τ_disc despite ongoing radial drift, fragmentation, and possible replenishment of the small-grain population.

Provide either an explicit characterization of such a viable region of parameter space or a proof that no such region exists.

