Background and setup. A vertex operator algebra (VOA) is a quadruple $(V,Y,\mathbf{1},\omega)$ where $V=\bigoplus_{n\in\mathbb{Z}}V_{(n)}$ is a $\mathbb{Z}$-graded vector space (with $\dim V_{(n)}<\infty$ and $V_{(n)}=0$ for $n$ sufficiently negative), $\mathbf{1}\in V_{(0)}$ is the vacuum, $\omega\in V_{(2)}$ is the conformal vector, and $Y(\cdot,x)\colon V\to(\mathrm{End}\,V)[[x,x^{-1}]]$ is the vertex operator map, satisfying the standard Jacobi identity, vacuum, creation, $L(-1)$-derivative, and Virasoro axioms.

A meromorphic open-string vertex algebra (MOSVA) is a $\mathbb{Z}$-graded vector space $V$ equipped with a vertex operator map $Y_V\colon V\otimes V\to V((x))$, a vacuum $\mathbf{1}$ and a conformal element $\omega$, satisfying the vacuum property, the $L(-1)$-derivative property, the Virasoro relations, and a weak associativity (rationality) axiom, but where the commutativity (skew-symmetry) of vertex operators is not required. Every VOA is in particular a MOSVA. A $V$-bimodule $W$ for a MOSVA $V$ is a $\mathbb{Z}$-graded vector space equipped with left and right vertex operator maps $Y^L_W\colon V\otimes W\to W((x))$ and $Y^R_W\colon W\otimes V\to W((x))$ compatible with the MOSVA structure (vacuum, $L(-1)$-derivative, weak associativities).

For a MOSVA $V$ and a $V$-bimodule $W$, there is a Hochschild-like cohomology $\widehat{H}^{n}_{\infty}(V,W)$ defined for each $n\in\mathbb{Z}_{+}$, where $n$-cochains are certain $W$-valued maps of $n$ variables in suitable spaces of formal/analytic series satisfying composability and convergence conditions, and the differential is the analogue of the Hochschild coboundary built from the left and right actions of $V$ on $W$.

Class of VOAs considered. Let $V$ be one of the following VOAs, viewed canonically as a MOSVA:
(a) the affine VOA $L_{\widehat{\mathfrak{g}}}(k,0)$ associated to a Wess–Zumino–Witten model at positive integer level $k$, for $\mathfrak{g}$ a finite-dimensional simple Lie algebra;
(b) a minimal model VOA $L(c_{p,q},0)$ of the Virasoro algebra at central charge $c_{p,q}=1-6(p-q)^2/(pq)$ with coprime integers $p,q\ge 2$;
(c) a lattice VOA $V_L$ associated to a positive-definite even lattice $L$;
(d) the moonshine module VOA $V^{\natural}$.

Question. Is it true that for every such $V$, every $V$-bimodule $W$ (in the MOSVA sense), and every positive integer $n$,
$$\widehat{H}^{n}_{\infty}(V,W)=0\,?$$

