Let $V = \bigoplus_{n \in \mathbb{Z}} V_{(n)}$ be a vertex operator algebra with vertex operator map $Y : V \otimes V \to V[[x, x^{-1}]]$ and vacuum $\mathbf{1}$. Assume:

(i) $V_{(0)} = \mathbb{C}\mathbf{1}$ and $V_{(n)} = 0$ for $n < 0$;
(ii) the contragredient module $V'$ is isomorphic to $V$ as a $V$-module;
(iii) $V$ is $C_2$-cofinite, i.e., $\dim V / C_2(V) < \infty$, where $C_2(V) = \mathrm{span}\{\mathrm{Res}_x\, x^{-2} Y(u,x) v : u, v \in V\}$;
(iv) every grading-restricted generalized $V$-module is completely reducible.

Let $G$ be a finite group of automorphisms of $V$. For each $g \in G$, consider the category of grading-restricted generalized $g$-twisted $V$-modules, and let $\mathcal{C}_G = \bigoplus_{g \in G} \mathcal{C}_g$ be the direct sum of these categories over all $g \in G$.

Question: Does $\mathcal{C}_G$ carry the structure of a $G$-crossed (braided) tensor category in the sense of Turaev, with the $g$-twisted modules forming the $g$-graded component, the tensor product given by twisted fusion (sending $\mathcal{C}_g \times \mathcal{C}_h$ to $\mathcal{C}_{gh}$), and a $G$-action permuting the homogeneous components?

