Let $V = \bigoplus_{n \ge 0} V_n$ be a vertex operator algebra over $\mathbb{C}$ satisfying the following three conditions:

(1) the central charge of $V$ equals $24$;
(2) every irreducible $V$-module is isomorphic to $V$ itself (i.e., $V$ is holomorphic);
(3) every $V$-module is completely reducible (i.e., $V$ is rational).

The homogeneous subspace $V_1$ of weight $1$ carries a Lie algebra structure given by the bracket $[a,b] = a_{(0)}b$, where $a_{(0)}$ denotes the zeroth mode of the vertex operator $Y(a,z)$.

Prove or disprove: any such $V$ is determined, up to isomorphism of vertex operator algebras, by the isomorphism class of the Lie algebra $V_1$. Equivalently, if $V$ and $V'$ both satisfy (1)–(3) and $V_1 \cong V'_1$ as Lie algebras, then $V \cong V'$ as vertex operator algebras.

