Let $M$ be a compact $8$-dimensional manifold with holonomy contained in $\mathrm{Spin}(7)$. Associated to $M$ one has:

(a) the Spin(7) elliptic genus $\mathrm{Ell}_M(\tau,\alpha)$, a two-variable modular-type invariant of $M$;

(b) the Shatashvili–Vafa Spin(7) superconformal vertex algebra $\mathcal{SV}^{\mathrm{Spin}(7)}$, whose irreducible unitary representations have well-defined characters (conjecturally given by certain mock modular forms);

(c) the chiral de Rham complex $\Omega^{\mathrm{ch}}_M$ of $M$, a sheaf of vertex superalgebras on $M$, together with a conjectural embedding of $\mathcal{SV}^{\mathrm{Spin}(7)}$ into the vertex algebra of global sections $C^\infty(M,\Omega^{\mathrm{ch}}_M)$ that is compatible with the Spin(7) structure;

(d) a distinguished odd element $Q^-_0$ acting on $C^\infty(M,\Omega^{\mathrm{ch}}_M)$, whose cohomology $H\big(C^\infty(M,\Omega^{\mathrm{ch}}_M),Q^-_0\big)$ inherits an action of $\mathcal{SV}^{\mathrm{Spin}(7)}$ and whose graded character recovers $\mathrm{Ell}_M(\tau,\alpha)$.

Question. Is the decomposition of $\mathrm{Ell}_M(\tau,\alpha)$ into characters of $\mathcal{SV}^{\mathrm{Spin}(7)}$ induced by a decomposition of the cohomology $H\big(C^\infty(M,\Omega^{\mathrm{ch}}_M),Q^-_0\big)$ into irreducible $\mathcal{SV}^{\mathrm{Spin}(7)}$-representations? Equivalently, do the multiplicity spaces appearing in the character decomposition of $\mathrm{Ell}_M(\tau,\alpha)$ arise as the multiplicity spaces of irreducible $\mathcal{SV}^{\mathrm{Spin}(7)}$-summands of this $Q^-_0$-cohomology?

